Limit returns nil when errors.Is(err, strconv.ErrRange) holds, otherwise the ParseInt
error unchanged. strconv.ErrRange (wrapped in *strconv.NumError) must NOT be in the
set; strconv.ErrSyntax and the opaque base/bitSize errors stay under
*strconv.NumError.Unwrap, without "possibly handled" marks. (The unwrapped
internal/strconv.Error entries are the toolchain over-approximation described in
port_wrap_numerror.)
-- args --
config/config.go:@limit
